[node name="KillBox" type="Area3D" parent="."]
editor_description = "The kill box under the arena. Everything that walks in PANOPTICON walks on one of two surfaces, the deck annulus (r35-r60) and the guard's platform (r8), both at y=0 with a twelve metre hole between them -- and, since the deck was given pits, with four more holes cut straight through the deck itself. This is what is under all of it.\n\nRADIUS 62, NOT 35, AND THAT IS THE WHOLE OF THE PIT MECHANIC. The courtyard is only r=35; the pits are at r=39.25 and r=49.25, outboard of it. A volume that stopped at r=35 would let a prisoner drop through a pit and fall forever, alive, past the bottom of the world -- the exact failure this node was built to end, reintroduced by a hole in the floor. So the roof now spans the arena out to the outer wall at r=62. Nothing is lost by that: the deck slab's underside is y=-1, this volume's roof is y=-3, and there is no walkable surface anywhere between them. The pits do not need a catcher of their own, and there is still exactly one place a fall is answered.\n\nIt is a trigger and nothing else: no collision of its own (layer 0, so nothing has to know it is here), monitorable off, and a mask of 1048577 (bit 0, the layer scenes/player/player.tscn puts a living body on, plus bit 20, MatchController.GHOST_HAZARD_LAYER, the layer a ghost stands on) so both a living prisoner and a ghost are seen falling in. The rifle cannot hit it -- default_weapon_profile.tres shoots with hit_areas off -- and a CharacterBody3D cannot stand on it.\n\nWHAT IT DOES IS NOT DECIDED HERE. scripts/match/kill_volume.gd resolves whatever entered it to a participant and hands it to MatchController.handle_fall(), which is the same node that already decides what a rifle hit means, and the same call the red traps make. The extent is on the script as three exported metres -- radius, how far under the deck the roof sits, how deep it goes -- and the child below is sized from them on ready, so the shape and the reasoning cannot disagree.\n\nPurely additive: no script here touches the arena, and deleting this node leaves the courtyard exactly as it was, a pit you can stand at the bottom of -- and the four deck pits a hole you fall through forever, which is why it is not deleted."
collision_layer = 0
collision_mask = 1048577
monitorable = false
script = ExtResource("2_kill_volume")
radius_metres = 62.0

[node name="Shape" type="CollisionShape3D" parent="KillBox"]
editor_description = "Deliberately empty. KillVolume._build_shape writes a CylinderShape3D over it on ready, from the exports on the parent, and places it hanging from the roof depth -- with the shipped numbers that is r=62 spanning y=-3 to y=-27, which starts below anything a jump can reach from either walking surface and ends well under the courtyard floor at -12.5 without going near the pen a converted body is parked in at -100."

