[node name="Traps" type="Node3D" parent="."]
editor_description = "Six red blocks that kill on contact, and the other half of the treachery the four Ring/Deck pits are. Read them together: at ten places round the lap the deck is now lethal a couple of metres off the racing line, six of them standing up in red and four of them holes in the floor.\n\nTHE RACING LINE IS NOT NARROWED. MatchRules.track_radius is 44.5 and the shipped RingRunner baseline has NO obstacle avoidance whatsoever -- it faces a point on the r=44.5 circle four metres ahead and holds full forward, for the whole lap. Anything standing on that circle would stop a bot dead and break the game. So every trap and every pit is placed flush against a boundary the arena ALREADY had: the inner ones stop at r=41.75 where the LaneInner cover band ends, the outer ones start at r=46.75 where the LaneMid cover band begins. The clear channel is r41.75-r46.75 exactly as it was before this node existed, and the bot still runs down the middle of it with 2.75 m of room inboard and 2.25 m outboard.\n\nANGLES. Runners go counter-clockwise from the start line at +4.8 deg. The first trap is at 56 deg, which is fifty degrees -- about forty metres -- of clear track for the field to converge out of the start line (where it is dealt across r41.5-r47.5) onto r=44.5 before anything can kill it. After that they alternate inner/outer roughly every thirty degrees and none is within eleven degrees of a cover piece, so no trap and no piece of cover ever fight for the same ground. The last thirty-seven degrees into the finish are clear.\n\nWHAT A TRAP DOES IS NOT DECIDED HERE, exactly as for KillBox: scripts/match/trap_volume.gd hands the body to MatchController.handle_fall(), which for a running prisoner in a round is MatchController.convert_participant() -- the same door the rifle kills through. Touching red and being shot are the same death. Each trap's mask is 1048577 (bit 0 plus bit 20, MatchController.GHOST_HAZARD_LAYER), so a ghost that wanders onto one is seen too -- handle_fall answers for it by placing it back at the start, since a ghost is already dead and cannot be killed a second time.\n\nPurely additive: the blocks carry no collision, so they are not cover, they occlude nothing, and the tower's sightlines are the ones that were tuned. Deleting this node leaves the arena exactly as it was."

[node name="Trap01_056deg" type="Area3D" parent="Traps"]
editor_description = "056 deg. Hugs the INNER shoulder at r=40.75, so it spans r39.75-r41.75 and stops dead on r=41.75 -- the radius the LaneInner cover band already ends at. The runners' clear channel r41.75-r46.75 is untouched.\n\nThe box is 5 m along the track, 2.2 m tall and 2 m deep. 2.2 m is the number that matters: the tuned MovementProfile jumps 1.11 m, so this cannot be hopped and has to be gone around."
collision_layer = 0
collision_mask = 1048577
monitorable = false
transform = Transform3D(0.82904, 0, 0.55919, 0, 1, 0, -0.55919, 0, 0.82904, 22.78711, 1.1, 33.78328)
script = ExtResource("3_trap_volume")
size_metres = Vector3(5.0, 2.2, 2.0)

[node name="Shape" type="CollisionShape3D" parent="Traps/Trap01_056deg"]
editor_description = "Deliberately empty. TrapVolume._build_shape writes a BoxShape3D over it on ready from size_metres on the parent."

[node name="Block" type="CSGBox3D" parent="Traps/Trap01_056deg"]
editor_description = "The red you see. use_collision is off on purpose -- a solid block would be new cover for the prisoners and a new occluder for the tower, and would give the avoidance-free runner brain something to grind against. It is sized by TrapVolume from the same size_metres the detection shape is, so the red and the kill cannot disagree."
material = SubResource("MatTrap")

